<<if $Random == 1>>
    There is nothing open on his computer, so you double click to open a web browser and are brought to a search engine. A rather boring homepage, but you guess <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> can’t but cool in every way. Though then you notice a pop-up in the upper right-hand corner asking if you would like to restore the last session. <span style="Color: Yellow">You instantly feel a knot in your stomach as you wonder just what <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> was looking at last time he used his computer, with many different, some unlikely, possibilities entering your brain.</span> <br>
    <br>
    Your curiosity gets the better of you as you click restore and are brought to a message board for boys your age. It mainly is about asking for homework help, recommending video games and comics, and the occasional post asking about partying up in an online game. <span style="Color: Pink">Though, curiously, the post <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> had opened is one asking if it was normally for boys to like other boys. You instantly feel your face heat up, wondering why he would click on such a thing, then suddenly feel your heart double its speed once you realize that the account that asked the question is the same account logged into the PC!</span> <br>

