<<elseif $Random == 3>>
    You stare at the blank desktop for a moment, the soft glow of his monitors calling your name, and click open the music player to scroll through the saved playlists. You had an idea of what type of music <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> listened too, expecting to see things you’ve heard him humming or even his dad tracks, though find quite a few with names like <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Gym Jams”</span>, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Chill Vibes”</span>, and <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Dad’s Greatest Hits”</span>. <span style="Color: LightGreen">You click on them and listen through as you continue to scroll; he has good taste.</span> <br>
    <br>
    Then you find something, a music file labeled <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“So Sorry (Unfinished)”</span>. <span style="Color: Yellow">Curiosity tugs at you, though you feel a knot in your chest, as if you’re invading something private, but click it before you can properly second-guess yourself.</span> <br>
    <br>
    The music begins softly – just a guitar – before <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s voice joins in. The lyrics catch you offguard, the raw pin you hear in his voice makes your chest tighten. As the song continues, you quickly piece together who it’s about: <span style="Color: Yellow">his mom. His words dance around the hurt and frustration of wanting to confront her but not being able to. Suddenly, the track cuts off mid-line, as if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> couldn’t finish it. <br>

